[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2578889595","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101318#issuecomment-2578889595","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101318","id":2578889595,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Ztrt7","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-08T23:43:34Z","updated_at":"2025-01-08T23:43:34Z","body":"So you're saying that this is fixed already in 4.4.dev2 and later? If so, are you reporting this to request that the fix be backported to 4.3.x?","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2578889595/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2579797482","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101318#issuecomment-2579797482","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101318","id":2579797482,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ZxJXq","user":{"login":"smix8","id":52464204,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDY0MjA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52464204?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8","html_url":"https://github.com/smix8","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-09T10:41:50Z","updated_at":"2025-01-09T11:00:18Z","body":"I am not convinced that Navigation is at fault here and not just what shows symptoms of other (core / script) threading issues.\n\nMy reasoning is:\n\n- There have been zero navigation changes between the version that show the bug and the version that does no longer show it. It is the identical navigation code. The only navigation change in 4.4 dev2 was adding the heap that only affects the pathfinding function, not the map_get_closest_point().\n\n- The far more demanding and complex pathfinding `get_path()` function runs without any issue in that same MRP on all versions. Both the get_path() and map_get_closest_point() use the same polygon graph in the search. Both use the very same `RWLock` as the other function.\n\n- The navigation map in the MRP does not change so there is zero meaningful write locking of anything, sure it locks on the physics step without doing anything, but all the time it is just increasing and decreasing the read lock counter of the internal RWLock.\n\nThe only noticeable difference in regards to threading between the two functions is that the `map_get_closest_point()` read-locks `twice` because it calls a subfunction that also locks as it can be called individually.\n\nSo I went ahead and compiled 4.3 stable, removed just the secondary RWLockRead() created by the inner subfunction, and indeed without the secondary `RWLockRead()` the bug does not show. So with that testing imo we have a culprit in the RWLock implementation of the core `RWLock` as having a 2+ read lock count is a valid use. I am unsure what magical fix was added in core that it does not show in later versions  @RandomShaper ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2579797482/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2580927399","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101318#issuecomment-2580927399","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101318","id":2580927399,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Z1dOn","user":{"login":"aromancev","id":29806368,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5ODA2MzY4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29806368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aromancev","html_url":"https://github.com/aromancev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aromancev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aromancev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aromancev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aromancev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aromancev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aromancev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aromancev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aromancev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aromancev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-09T17:53:53Z","updated_at":"2025-01-09T17:53:53Z","body":"@smix8 thank for taking look! I think you found it! I wasn't sure it's actually the nav server, but it's how I managed to reproduce it.\n\nBut before we blame `RWLock` I want to offer an alternative suggestion. Apologies, I have not looked at the implementation but it might not be a valid case to acquire two read locks twice as you've shown.\n\nThe reason is that in some RWLock implementations, two consecutive read locks can deadlock if a write lock happens between them on a different thread. A read lock can \"allow\" write to go first. This is done to prevent write starvation when read locks basically continuously keep it locked because they are allowed to acquire it at the same time.\n\nThis is the case in the standard RWLock implementation in Go, for example. You are not allowed to acquire read lock twice in the same goroutine. I think we should double-check if that's the case in the lock implementation use by Godot.\n\nAgain, apologies I don't have time to do it now, but I wanted to raise the question.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2580927399/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2580937776","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101318#issuecomment-2580937776","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101318","id":2580937776,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Z1fww","user":{"login":"aromancev","id":29806368,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5ODA2MzY4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29806368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aromancev","html_url":"https://github.com/aromancev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aromancev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aromancev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aromancev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aromancev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aromancev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aromancev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aromancev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aromancev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aromancev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-09T17:59:32Z","updated_at":"2025-01-09T17:59:32Z","body":"@akien-mga it seems it is not reproducible in 4.4-dev2, but there is nothing in the changelog about this so I assumed even if it was fixed, it was accidental. So I raised this issue because:\n1. If it's not fixed explicitly it might still be there, but the timing has changed and it's harder to reproduce. At least I found how to reproduce it and we can verify the reason. And it seems @smix8 actually found it.\n2. Someone else might encounter the issue and will find this conversation helpful.\n\nI don't know if we should back port the fix (I'm new to the Godot ecosystem) so I'll leave it for maintainers to decide. Just thought it would be useful.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2580937776/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2583662935","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101318#issuecomment-2583662935","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101318","id":2583662935,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Z_5FX","user":{"login":"aromancev","id":29806368,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5ODA2MzY4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29806368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aromancev","html_url":"https://github.com/aromancev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aromancev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aromancev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aromancev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aromancev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aromancev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aromancev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aromancev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aromancev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aromancev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-10T19:11:47Z","updated_at":"2025-01-10T19:12:22Z","body":"Just for context, `NavigationServer3D.set_active(false)` also fixes the issue. So there's definitely something happening in the nav server that triggers the deadlock. My suspicion it's that write lock in between two consecutive read locks.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2583662935/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2586359145","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101318#issuecomment-2586359145","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101318","id":2586359145,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6aKLVp","user":{"login":"RandomShaper","id":11797174,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzk3MTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11797174?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper","html_url":"https://github.com/RandomShaper","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-13T07:16:46Z","updated_at":"2025-01-13T07:16:46Z","body":"A given thread shouldn't re-lock `RWLock`, regardless whether both locks are for read. That'll invoke undefined behavior on the underlying implementation. Given how easy it's to fall into that trap, we may want to add some check for debug builds.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2586359145/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2624284980","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101318#issuecomment-2624284980","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101318","id":2624284980,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ca2k0","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6